o`/`sdn status` all show no EVE device or SDN was ever created) to be the identical byte-for-byte error — `evebuild/nightly:10.1.0-kvm-amd64` not found — as the three failures already diagnosed earlier in this run (`TestKvmToKRepartitionGeometry`, `TestBackupCorruptRestore`, `Shrink`), so it shares the same root cause: `PersistTooFull` calls `requirePinnedInitialVersion` with `INITIAL_EVE_VERSION=10.1.0`, which resolves through the unset `initialEVERepoParamKey` and defaults to the `evebuild/nightly` nightly-build repo — a repo that only holds numeric build-id tags, not semantic release tags like `10.1.0-kvm-amd64` — so the pull always fails in setup before any device/SDN provisioning. This is a known, recurring issue: the exact same `PersistTooFull` failure (identical signature) is already logged in this run's own ledger on 2026-10-29 (run #1), alongside four other konvert tests, meaning it's been a recurring environment/test-config gap since at least that date, not a new regression or code defect.","time":{"start":1793575319000,"stop":1793575340390,"duration":21390}}]},"tags":[]},"source":"998622fe7f5b2998.json","parameterValues":[]}